<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Transformations of the tangent graph</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text>Consider the function

\(f(x)=2\tan\left(x-\frac{\pi}{4}\right)+1.\)

The graph below shows the transformed tangent function. Use it to identify the transformations and key features.

[[jsxgraph]]
var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {
    boundingbox: [-3.5, 5, 3.5, -3],
    axis: true,
    showCopyright: false,
    keepAspectRatio: false
});

var f = function(x) {
    return 2*Math.tan(x-Math.PI/4)+1;
};

board.create('functiongraph', [f, -Math.PI+0.05, -Math.PI/4-0.08], {
    strokeWidth: 2
});

board.create('functiongraph', [f, -Math.PI/4+0.08, 3*Math.PI/4-0.08], {
    strokeWidth: 2
});

board.create('functiongraph', [f, 3*Math.PI/4+0.08, Math.PI-0.05], {
    strokeWidth: 2
});

board.create('line', [[-Math.PI/4, -3], [-Math.PI/4, 5]], {
    dash: 2,
    strokeColor: '#C0392B'
});

board.create('line', [[3*Math.PI/4, -3], [3*Math.PI/4, 5]], {
    dash: 2,
    strokeColor: '#C0392B'
});

board.create('point', [Math.PI/4, 1], {
    name: 'Centre',
    size: 4,
    fixed: true,
    color: '#239B56'
});
[[/jsxgraph]]

1. Vertical scale factor

Enter the value of \(a\).

[[input:ans_a]]
[[validation:ans_a]] [[feedback:prt1]]

2. Horizontal translation

Enter the value of \(h\) in the form \(f(x)=a\tan(x-h)+k\).

[[input:ans_h]]
[[validation:ans_h]] [[feedback:prt2]]

3. Vertical translation

Enter the value of \(k\).

[[input:ans_k]]
[[validation:ans_k]] [[feedback:prt3]]

4. Vertical asymptotes

Enter the left asymptote nearest the origin.

[[input:ans_asymL]]
[[validation:ans_asymL]]

Enter the right asymptote nearest the origin.

[[input:ans_asymR]]
[[validation:ans_asymR]] [[feedback:prt4]]

5. Centre point

Enter the \(x\)-coordinate of the centre.

[[input:ans_centre_x]]
[[validation:ans_centre_x]]

Enter the \(y\)-coordinate of the centre.

[[input:ans_centre_y]]
[[validation:ans_centre_y]] [[feedback:prt5]]</text>
